module

public import TauCeti.Algebra.Module.ZLattice.Determinant

/-!
# Integral lattices have covolume at least one

An integral full lattice `Λ` in a finite-dimensional real inner product space has covolume at
least one: its squared covolume is its determinant `ZLattice.det Λ`, the order of its
discriminant group, which is at least one.

In the uniqueness argument of Cohn and Elkies this bounds from below the covolume of the lattice
generated by the translated centers of an optimal periodic packing; together with the unit center
density of the packing, it squeezes that covolume to one.

## Main statements

* `ZLattice.IsIntegral.one_le_covolume`: an integral full lattice has covolume at least one.

## References

* H. Cohn and N. Elkies, *New upper bounds on sphere packings I*, Annals of Mathematics 157
  (2003), 689–714, Section 8.
-/

public section

open MeasureTheory

/-- An integral full lattice has covolume at least one. -/
theorem ZLattice.IsIntegral.one_le_covolume {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E]
    [InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]
    {Λ : Submodule ℤ E} [DiscreteTopology Λ] [IsZLattice ℝ Λ] (h : ZLattice.IsIntegral Λ) :
    1 ≤ ZLattice.covolume Λ := by
  -- The squared covolume is the determinant, which is at least one.
  have hdet := h.one_le_det
  rw [ZLattice.det_def] at hdet
  nlinarith [ZLattice.covolume_pos Λ volume]
